ped per-invocation proxy, not filterwarnings","_lib_warn.py:74-76 docstring: 'Suppressing it with a scoped, per-invocation guard — rather than a process-global filterwarnings(\\'ignore\\', ...) — keeps the field the single advisory WITHOUT silencing the warning for unrelated import rebar callers sharing the process.'","mcp_server.py:700 comment explicitly warns the process-global filter 'would silence CrossSessionWarning for other import-rebar callers sharing this process'"],"finding":"The plan asserts MCP single-emit dedup is done via a process-wide filterwarnings('ignore', CrossSessionWarning) installed in build_server(); the codebase refutes this — it uses a scoped per-tool suppress_library_double_advisory(mcp) proxy and its docstring explicitly rejects the process-global filter because it would silence CrossSessionWarning for unrelated import-rebar callers sharing the process.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f69852e6e9b23e86e","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach 'Surface layering' bullet (MCP); Scope 'src/rebar/mcp_server.py'; Testing / dedup discussion","norm_id":"nf2c651b7139e2077","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An import-rebar embedder running inside the same process as the MCP server would have its own CrossSessionWarning silenced if the plan's process-wide filter were implemented","AC line for MCP dedup would be validated against the wrong mechanism"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In build_server(), wrap read/write tool registrars with a scoped suppress_cross_session_warning() proxy (suppress_library_double_advisory) rather than installing a process-global filterwarnings, so the MCP response field is the single advisory without affecting other in-process rebar callers.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Replace the MCP process-wide `filterwarnings(\"ignore\", CrossSessionWarning)` with a scoped per-invocation guard that wraps each MCP tool in `suppress_cross_session_warning()`, so the response field stays the single MCP advisory WITHOUT silencing CrossSessionWarning for other `import rebar` callers sharing the process; state this blast-radius rationale in the plan.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"MCP (src/rebar/mcp_server.py) — build_server() installs a process-wide filterwarnings(\\\"ignore\\\", CrossSessionWarning), so the response field is the only MCP advisory in the running server.\"","A structurally-different alternative wraps each MCP tool in the existing suppress_cross_session_warning() guard, scoping suppression to the tool call rather than the whole process — same single-advisory outcome, far smaller blast radius.","The plan states only a positive-outcome assertion for the process-wide choice and does not address shared-process library callers; no rationale weighs it against a scoped guard.","Codebase evidence the scoped approach is feasible and preferred: mcp_server.py:698-706 registers read/write tools through suppress_library_double_advisory(mcp) with the comment 'a scoped guard makes the field the single advisory without a process-global warnings filter (which would silence CrossSessionWarning for other import-rebar callers sharing this process)'; _lib_warn.py:67-109 implements this per-invocation proxy."],"finding":"The plan's MCP single-emit dedup mechanism (process-wide filterwarnings('ignore', CrossSessionWarning) in build_server()) is a clearly-inferior alternative to a scoped per-invocation guard: a process-global filter silences CrossSessionWarning for unrelated `import rebar` callers that share the MCP server process, over-suppressing the very library channel this story adds.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fac32b1c01dc1fe15","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Surface layering, MCP bullet; Scope → src/rebar/mcp_server.py: \"build_server() ignores CrossSessionWarning process-wide\"","norm_id":"n8539fcdae90436c6","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A host process embeds the rebar MCP server AND makes direct `import rebar` single-ticket calls: the process-wide filter swallows the CrossSessionWarning those direct callers rely on.","A test or tool that builds the server and then exercises library functions in the same interpreter sees CrossSessionWarning globally suppressed."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In build_server(), register the read/write tool clusters through a suppressing proxy that runs each tool body under suppress_cross_session_warning() (per-invocation), instead of installing a process-global warnings filter; update the Approach → Surface layering MCP bullet and Scope accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Replace the process-wide `filterwarnings('ignore', CrossSessionWarning)` in the MCP dedup with a scoped suppression (e.g. wrap tool dispatch in `suppress_cross_session_warning()` / a per-server proxy) so library callers sharing the process still receive a filterable `CrossSessionWarning`, and state in the plan why a global filter is rejected.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'MCP (src/rebar/mcp_server.py) — build_server() installs a process-wide filterwarnings(\"ignore\", CrossSessionWarning), so the response field is the only MCP advisory in the running server.'","Story goal (Context): the first-class way to raise the warning for `import rebar` callers is Python's warnings subsystem 'so callers can filter/escalate it with stdlib filters' — a process-wide ignore filter negates this for co-resident library callers.","warnings.filterwarnings resolves (Verified) — the mechanism is runnable, so the gap is correctness/scope, not existence.","A scoped alternative is achievable and demonstrated as a per-server proxy (rebar._lib_warn.suppress_library_double_advisory resolves) rather than a process-global filter — evidence the process-wide approach is not the only, nor the safest, achievable design."],"finding":"The MCP dedup mechanism the plan specifies — build_server() installing a process-wide filterwarnings('ignore', CrossSessionWarning) — is technically runnable but carries an unstated capability gap: a process-global warnings filter also silences the library CrossSessionWarning for any other `import rebar` caller sharing the MCP server process, which defeats this story's stated purpose of giving library callers a filterable/escalatable warning.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1d363faca8c6ac39","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Surface layering (MCP bullet); Scope: src/rebar/mcp_server.py","norm_id":"nbf7974eaed71d661","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An MCP server process that also hosts or imports rebar as a library for another in-process caller: that caller's CrossSessionWarning is permanently suppressed by the global filter.","A test or embedding that runs build_server() then later exercises import-rebar functions expecting to observe/escalate CrossSessionWarning."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the Surface layering MCP bullet and Scope, specify that build_server() runs each read/write tool under suppress_cross_session_warning() (a scoped guard) rather than installing a process-global warnings filter, so the response field remains the single MCP advisory without silencing CrossSessionWarning for other import-rebar callers in the same process.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Replace the proposed process-wide `filterwarnings(\"ignore\", CrossSessionWarning)` in `build_server()` with a scoped per-invocation guard (`suppress_cross_session_warning()` per tool call, e.g. the existing `suppress_library_double_advisory` proxy) so only the MCP response path is deduped and other in-process `import rebar` consumers still receive the warning.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"build_server() installs a process-wide filterwarnings(\\\"ignore\\\", CrossSessionWarning), so the response field is the only MCP advisory\"","Codebase has the narrower alternative: src/rebar/_lib_warn.py:67 suppress_library_double_advisory wraps each tool in a scoped suppress_cross_session_warning() 'rather than a process-global filterwarnings(\\'ignore\\', ...)'","mcp_server.py:699-701 documents the deliberate rejection: 'a scoped guard makes the field the single advisory without a process-global warnings filter (which would silence CrossSessionWarning for other import-rebar callers sharing this process)'","tests/unit/test_cross_session_lib.py:307 test_mcp_build_server_does_not_globally_silence_cross_session_warning is RED against exactly the process-global filter the plan proposes"],"finding":"The plan proposes an MCP dedup via a process-wide filterwarnings(\"ignore\", CrossSessionWarning) in build_server(), a coarse mechanism that silences the warning for every in-process `import rebar` consumer, not just the MCP response path; a narrower scoped guard is the intended design and already exists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f066b62ffa611b9f2","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach > Surface layering (MCP bullet); Scope > src/rebar/mcp_server.py","norm_id":"n8fc9c657b25713a7","priority":0.85,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A host process runs both an MCP server and other `import rebar` code sharing the interpreter: the global filter suppresses legitimate CrossSessionWarnings for the non-MCP callers"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the MCP surface bullet and Scope, register read/write tools through a per-invocation `suppress_cross_session_warning()` wrapper instead of a process-global `filterwarnings` install; keep the response field as the single MCP advisory without altering the warnings filter for the shared process.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"bl